        "original_id": "65055dd5-ba79-5d21-8c0c-b02383e65551",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Hires Root Beer, Vernors Ginger Ale\n- People: James Vernor, Charles Elmer Hires\n- Places: Detroit, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania\n- Roles: pharmacist, Quaker\n\nFacts:\n- In 1866, James Vernor created Vernors Ginger Ale in Detroit.\n- Vernors Ginger Ale dates to 1866.\n- Vernors Ginger Ale is older than Hires Root Beer.\n- Charles Elmer Hires was a Quaker pharmacist from Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.\n- Charles Elmer Hires formulated the beverage Hires Root Beer, which was named after him.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "e53f4967-cafe-5ef2-b4b1-85806fdeee36",
        "text": "Page: Hires Root Beer. Sentence: Only Vernors Ginger Ale , dating to 1866, is older.\nPage: Vernors. Sentence: It was created in 1866 by James Vernor, a Detroit pharmacist.\nPage: Charles Elmer Hires. Sentence: He was a Quaker pharmacist from Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, who formulated the eponymous Hires Root Beer beverage.",
